{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00433",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.04,
      "end_seconds": 4.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor. They're in and comfortable, and I have the measurements ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.36,
      "end_seconds": 8.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.83,
      "end_seconds": 14.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "I wanted to get a fever for days looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.83,
      "end_seconds": 18.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.2,
      "end_seconds": 31.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.57,
      "text": "Um, about... well, two days. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.43,
      "end_seconds": 42.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse. These questions might sound routine, but they matter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.28,
      "end_seconds": 47.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "It's moderate, honestly. It happens once or twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.2,
      "end_seconds": 50.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Have you had constipation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.07,
      "end_seconds": 59.88,
      "duration_seconds": 7.81,
      "text": "Yeah. About a week, I'd say. I was feeling weak at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.34,
      "end_seconds": 64.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.15,
      "end_seconds": 65.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.74,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.54,
      "end_seconds": 84.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Have you had any vomiting, rash or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.93,
      "end_seconds": 90.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "I haven't had vomiting, rash or blood in the stool, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.17,
      "end_seconds": 93.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Has there been any cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.36,
      "end_seconds": 97.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any cough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.02,
      "end_seconds": 101.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.61,
      "end_seconds": 103.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.26,
      "end_seconds": 120.65,
      "duration_seconds": 16.39,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.73,
      "end_seconds": 125.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.7,
      "end_seconds": 129.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.36,
      "end_seconds": 131.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "My sister has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.29,
      "end_seconds": 135.47,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.62,
      "end_seconds": 147.92,
      "duration_seconds": 11.3,
      "text": "Not at the moment, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.84,
      "end_seconds": 150.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.03,
      "end_seconds": 153.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.09,
      "end_seconds": 156.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Let me just write this down properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.49,
      "end_seconds": 171.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Right, carry on. What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.54,
      "end_seconds": 177.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "I've had diabetes, yes. I've had an enlarged prostate for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.8,
      "end_seconds": 185.94,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "Right, so that's your known diabetes. We'll keep that in mind today. Okay, an enlarged prostate, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.55,
      "end_seconds": 189.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.69,
      "end_seconds": 190.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.45,
      "end_seconds": 209.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.06,
      "end_seconds": 213.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "It's glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 214.45,
      "end_seconds": 218.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 4 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.73,
      "end_seconds": 222.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.49,
      "end_seconds": 233.42,
      "duration_seconds": 9.93,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. I take tamsulosin, 0.4 milligrams, at night. I'm on Dolo, 650 milligrams, when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.58,
      "end_seconds": 238.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Sorry, I'm just writing a few notes, bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.85,
      "end_seconds": 242.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Um, uh, no problem, take your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.27,
      "end_seconds": 244.2,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.71,
      "end_seconds": 246.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.8,
      "end_seconds": 255.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.3,
      "end_seconds": 266.75,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 267.21,
      "end_seconds": 274.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pressure 121 over 75, pulse is 92 beats a minute, temperature 38.8. Saturation 97 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.93,
      "end_seconds": 279.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Thanks. Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.1,
      "end_seconds": 281.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.4,
      "end_seconds": 285.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.86,
      "end_seconds": 288.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.84,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.41,
      "end_seconds": 302.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "I can't feel your liver or spleen enlarged."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.14,
      "end_seconds": 305.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Okay, now bend it for me, slowly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.89,
      "end_seconds": 320.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Your tummy is a bit full and tender in the lower part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 323.07,
      "end_seconds": 334.69,
      "duration_seconds": 11.62,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.27,
      "end_seconds": 339.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.95,
      "end_seconds": 340.67,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.27,
      "end_seconds": 363.22,
      "duration_seconds": 12.95,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Okay, so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with typhoid fever, which we need to confirm at this stage. I can't rule out a viral illness yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 364.15,
      "end_seconds": 368.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.72,
      "end_seconds": 389.01,
      "duration_seconds": 19.29,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now typhoid fever, which we need to confirm is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a fever for days for two days, moderate, and no rash or blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 390.11,
      "end_seconds": 391.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.91,
      "end_seconds": 395.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Okay, has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.76,
      "end_seconds": 412.48,
      "duration_seconds": 16.72,
      "text": "Okay, so not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.91,
      "end_seconds": 419.12,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange blood cultures for prolonged fever. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.78,
      "end_seconds": 423.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.37,
      "end_seconds": 428.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a full blood count for fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.93,
      "end_seconds": 430.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 431.53,
      "end_seconds": 454.65,
      "duration_seconds": 23.12,
      "text": "Eat only home-cooked food and drink boiled or bottled water while this is going on. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 455.39,
      "end_seconds": 456.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 458.03,
      "end_seconds": 465.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the fever stays high or the tummy pain gets sharp."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 466.31,
      "end_seconds": 468.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 471.85,
      "end_seconds": 477.69,
      "duration_seconds": 5.84,
      "text": "Come back in three days. Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 478.68,
      "end_seconds": 482.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "So, I come back in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 483.6,
      "end_seconds": 488.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 489.51,
      "end_seconds": 492.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}